# A verdict SOT that only documents green

#1884's own starting state, and the floor under the derived subject list.

The guard picks its second-check subjects out of the sweep rather than a
hand-written array, because an array is deleted one line at a time and takes the
file out of the check with it (#1875). Derivation has the mirrored failure: drop
the red branch from a file and it simply stops being a subject, and an empty
derived set is green.

So the three paths #1884 names are a floor on that set. Here `.codex` documents
only green — nothing else in the tree is wrong — and the floor is the only thing
that can notice.
